``` 1) FOUND / NOT FOUND report for every path in the list. Change index=<your_index> and the time range. ```
| tstats count latest(_time) as last_seen where index=<your_index> earliest=-7d by source host
| stats sum(count) as events max(last_seen) as last_seen values(host) as hosts by source
| append
    [| makeresults
     | eval source=split("/app/ICM_CPW/log/ap/default.log,/app/log/ap/default.log,/app/ICM_CPW/log/sh/default.log,/app/log/ap/monitoringTarget.log,/IFDATA/DATA/GE/LOG/SH/default.log,/IFDATA/DATA/PC/LOG/PISP2/pisp2.log,/opt/HULFT/etc/trace,/opt/HULFT/etc/BatchLog/HUL_JOB.LOG,/opt/plat/logs/pltcomm.log,/var/opt/universal/log/unv.log", ",")
     | mvexpand source
     | eval wanted=1
     | fields source wanted]
| eval key=lower(source)
| stats sum(events) as events max(last_seen) as last_seen values(hosts) as hosts max(wanted) as wanted values(source) as source by key
| where wanted=1
| eval status=if(events>0, "FOUND", "NOT FOUND"), last_seen=strftime(last_seen, "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")
| table status source events last_seen hosts
| sort status source

``` 2) Same list, but also catch rotated or renamed files (default.log.1, default.log.20261001, ...) ```
| tstats count latest(_time) as last_seen where index=<your_index> earliest=-7d
    (source="/app/ICM_CPW/log/ap/default.log*" OR source="/app/log/ap/default.log*" OR source="/app/ICM_CPW/log/sh/default.log*"
     OR source="/app/log/ap/monitoringTarget.log*" OR source="/IFDATA/DATA/GE/LOG/SH/default.log*" OR source="/IFDATA/DATA/PC/LOG/PISP2/pisp2.log*"
     OR source="/opt/HULFT/etc/trace*" OR source="/opt/HULFT/etc/BatchLog/HUL_JOB.LOG*" OR source="/opt/plat/logs/pltcomm.log*"
     OR source="/var/opt/universal/log/unv.log*")
    by source host sourcetype
| eval last_seen=strftime(last_seen, "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")

``` 3) Not in your index? See which index they actually land in (needs access to those indexes) ```
| tstats count latest(_time) as last_seen where index=* earliest=-7d
    source IN ("/app/ICM_CPW/log/ap/default.log", "/app/log/ap/default.log", "/app/ICM_CPW/log/sh/default.log",
               "/app/log/ap/monitoringTarget.log", "/IFDATA/DATA/GE/LOG/SH/default.log", "/IFDATA/DATA/PC/LOG/PISP2/pisp2.log",
               "/opt/HULFT/etc/trace", "/opt/HULFT/etc/BatchLog/HUL_JOB.LOG", "/opt/plat/logs/pltcomm.log", "/var/opt/universal/log/unv.log")
    by index source
| eval last_seen=strftime(last_seen, "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")

``` 4) All-time view from index metadata (first and last time each source was seen) ```
| metadata type=sources index=<your_index>
| search source IN ("/app/ICM_CPW/log/ap/default.log", "/app/log/ap/default.log", "/app/ICM_CPW/log/sh/default.log",
                    "/app/log/ap/monitoringTarget.log", "/IFDATA/DATA/GE/LOG/SH/default.log", "/IFDATA/DATA/PC/LOG/PISP2/pisp2.log",
                    "/opt/HULFT/etc/trace", "/opt/HULFT/etc/BatchLog/HUL_JOB.LOG", "/opt/plat/logs/pltcomm.log", "/var/opt/universal/log/unv.log")
| eval firstTime=strftime(firstTime, "%F %T"), lastTime=strftime(lastTime, "%F %T"), recentTime=strftime(recentTime, "%F %T")
| table source totalCount firstTime lastTime recentTime

``` 5) NOT FOUND? Is the forwarder even watching the file? (forwarder's own logs) ```
index=_internal sourcetype=splunkd (component=TailingProcessor OR component=WatchedFile OR component=TailReader)
    ("/opt/HULFT/etc/trace" OR "/app/log/ap/default.log" OR "unv.log" OR "pltcomm.log" OR "pisp2.log" OR "HUL_JOB.LOG")
| table _time host component log_level _raw

``` 6) Forwarder throughput per file (metrics.log keeps only the busiest sources by default) ```
index=_internal source=*metrics.log group=per_source_thruput
    (series="/app/*" OR series="/IFDATA/*" OR series="/opt/HULFT/*" OR series="/opt/plat/*" OR series="/var/opt/universal/*")
| stats sum(kb) as kb latest(_time) as last_seen by host series
| eval last_seen=strftime(last_seen, "%F %T")
